## Lore

The adarok, the Flying Mountain, is a forty-foot giant with legs and great wings that looks like a demon, or a sliver of mountain come to demonic life. In spite of that face it is a kind and gentle creature that hates to kill or cause pain, feeding mostly on leaves, fruit and vegetables and only rarely on animals or fish; only the most evil rogue eats intelligent beings. Provoked or frustrated, though, an adarok can uproot trees, smash buildings and hurl vehicles like toys, and its supernatural strength, Glitter Boy grade hide and imperviousness to fire make it a devastating fighter.

It has few natural enemies, but the Splugorth and their minions enslave it, and humans and D-Bees often attack it on sight, mistaking it for a demon. The giants would rather calm their attackers or simply leave than fight. That prejudice saddens them, but they are used to it and tolerant of others'' failings. They befriend anyone of a similar alignment who treats them with respect.

Adarok are not dimensional travelers; any found off their homeworld were brought by slavers or mages or fell through a rift. They are sold as slaves in Atlantis and wander its forests as escapees, and small communities are known in England, the forests of eastern Canada and the jungles of Asia. They prefer forests and jungles and avoid desolation. Dull grey to brown with pale green splotches, with a monstrous fanged head, three-toed clawed feet, a hunched back, giant wings and a short tail.

Alignment: any, but typically good or selfish. Weight 18 to 28 tons; 40 to 60 ft (12.2 to 18.3 m) tall. Average experience level 1D4+1. Average life span 800 years. Slave market value four to ten million credits.

## GM Notes

Enemies: the Splugorth and their minions, magic users who enslave other creatures, and most supernatural beings, who see the adarok as a rival or threat. It does not hate humans or humanoids, even those who attack it.
